{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110950","id":2865899445,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6q0ie1","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110950","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110950.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110950.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110950","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110950/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110950/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110950/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/0a8090a9975ef274b0e27239d4d80745c8632a06","number":110950,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"GDScript: Add support for `@read_only` annotation","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm","html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"* closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/13285\r\n* requires #85481 (sort of, see below)\r\n* Merge notes: contains overlapping/duplicated code in `GDScriptAnalyzer::reduce_call` and `GDScriptAnalyzer::reduce_assignment` with #111089 \r\n\r\nThe user can define a class variable as `@read_only`. \r\n* That variable must then be given a value, either in-line or in the constructor. \r\n  * Constructor assignment without #85481 would be \"unsafe\", as the base constructor will not necessarily be called, resulting in a \"not initialized\" (i.e. default value) variable\r\n* Constructor assignment is only possible in the constructor of the class where the variable is declared. \r\n* This supports non-pure initializers, as GDScript does. \r\n* This variable cannot be accessed before being initialized in constructor if not initialized inline\r\n  * Same caveat applies as above in event where base constructor is not called\r\n* This variable cannot have a setter defined (would be useless) but can have a getter defined\r\n\r\nIf the user wishes to give it a value at a child class level, this is achieved by passing it as an argument to the base class' constructor. \r\n\r\n\r\nSee example in proposal. \r\n\r\nTO-DO:\r\n- [x] Improve the constructor check. Currently it doesn't take into account if/match statements, which may result in unassigned variables\r\n\r\n~\r\n\r\nFor immutable variables (similar, but can only be assigned in-line and cannot have a getter), see #111089 \r\nThose can also be used as locals and parameters to functions","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097162,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTcxNjI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/discussion","name":"discussion","description":"","color":"ccaaff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id"